    "optional_if_unreported": true,
    "notes": "Catch-all current liabilities filed under us-gaap:OtherLiabilitiesCurrent (e.g., AAPL's $78B FY24). EDGAR-only — intentionally NO fmp_field. FMP's `otherCurrentLiabilities` field has DIFFERENT scope: it's typically narrower than EDGAR's `OtherLiabilitiesCurrent` because FMP separately surfaces `taxPayables`, `capitalLeaseObligationsCurrent`, etc. (For AAPL FY24: FMP otherCurrentLiabilities=50,071M, EDGAR OtherLiabilitiesCurrent=78,304M, difference=28,233M ≈ FMP taxPayables 26,601 + FMP capitalLeaseObligationsCurrent 1,632.) Routing through FMP would also risk prepaid-style scope creep when other concepts fall back to FMP otherCurrentLiabilities. EDGAR-only keeps semantics tight: only filers whose 10-K explicitly tags OtherLiabilitiesCurrent populate this row; if unreported, leave it blank and let balance-sheet subline diagnostics catch any residual section gap. Bound to `tpl.fm.balance_sheet.current_liability_2` synthetic row inserted via _insert_other_current_liabilities_row in template_builder.py."
  },
